dossier='''# Fully rough hypoplastic granular interface

This is the Stutz–Mašín–Wuttke2016 fully rough HvWE interface, evaluated with its explicitly inherited original von Wolffersdorff1996 host. It is a source-reconciled realization: duplicated stress/density factors and the pressure sign in the2016 host print are corrected against readable primary1996 equations. The author2016 thesis is visually verified; an exact original2016 article visual receipt remains unavailable. The complete source/version inventory and independent approval retain that distinction.

The laboratory controls normal compression strain and two source shear angles along a dimensionless path. Local effective Cauchy stresses and void ratio evolve in fixed local axes with zero spin. The four-stress embedding recovers Mandel [σnormal,σplane,σplane,√2τx,0,√2τz]; shear stretching is half the corresponding angle derivative. Lateral stress evolves even though its stretching is zero. The generic adaptive midpoint integrator and rollback/restart protocol are Atlas numerical choices. Initial stresses, density, controls, coordinate and parameters must be complete. No memory is reset at reversal.

All eight host parameters retain their source meaning. The example uses original1996 Hochstetten soil constants with an illustrative initial state; this is not an interface calibration or experiment reproduction. p_ref is a numerical stress scale and sets a small positive pressure admission margin; ordered limiting densities, a positive-definite compressive stress and real regular factors are required. Exact isotropy uses the source limit F=1, with no epsilon or invented Lode direction.

The independently accepted bounded study includes ten matrix-reference paths, eleven increments, both shear directions, normal loading/extension, holds, reversal, isotropy, near-isotropy and existing shear. All five state components and six recovered stresses are checked. Native/Wasm each passed59 frozen requests, including rejection, complete rollback, recovery and restart, with strict full-component parity. Approval covers this mathematical/interface scope, not experimental validation or the entire parameter domain. The original nonfinite-assessor defect and its pre-execution correction are retained.

No finite-slip/thickness adapter, CNL/CNS apparatus solver, finite-spin transport, opening/recontact, roughness degradation or pore-pressure law is supplied. The prescribed shear angles are not silently replaced with displacement divided by layer thickness. Later roughness/history variants remain distinct.

Sources: [Stutz, Mašín and Wuttke2016](https://doi.org/10.1007/s11440-016-0440-1), [author thesis](https://www.geotechnics.ifg.uni-kiel.de/en/publications/2016-hanshenningstutz.pdf), and original1996 von Wolffersdorff equations retained by exact source receipt. Raw copyrighted PDFs and author binaries are not distributed or executed. Full provenance is in docs/ingestion/hypoplastic-interface-2016/source-v2/; accepted checklist in catalogue/agent-reviews/hvwe2016-reconciled-fixed-local-agent-v1.json.
'''
